mission "A Chart Beneath the Bell"
    name "A Chart Beneath the Bell"
    description "A salvager has recovered a bell-shaped brass token from a wreck that should be three hundred years old."
    source "Wreckers' Moon"
    destination "Bellweather Cay"
    reward 680
    speaker offer "Marda Quill"
    speaker visit "Marda Quill"
    speaker complete "Marda Quill"
    to offer
        has "A Sea Without Masters: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `A salvager lays a bell-shaped brass token on Marda Quill's table. It is green with age, and the wreck it came from should have been under the sea for three centuries.`
            `Marda turns the token between two fingers. "The metal is old enough. The question is why an expedition that should have vanished from memory left a mark somebody still recognises."`
            choice
                `"I will lend a hand. Tell me where to begin."`
                    accept
                `"There is more here than you have told me. What is it?"`
                    goto details
                `"I will not put my crew between old enemies."`
                    close
            label details
                `Marda slides an old chart toward you. "Someone has taken great care to remove this voyage from the books. I want to know what they were so anxious to hide."`
                choice
                    `"Then you have my word. I will see it through."`
                        accept
                    `"Then we part here. Fair winds."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Chart Beneath the Bell. A salvager has recovered a bell-shaped brass token from a wreck that should be three hundred years old."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Bellweather Cay, Marda matches the token against the marks on her chart. "This is no merchant's tally. The expedition was searching for a place someone had taken off every official chart—not simply another pile of gold."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Marda wraps the chart in oilcloth. "A good find, captain, but not a comfortable one. Every answer points to another hand that would rather this story stayed buried. The people of these islands deserve the truth before a crown or company claims it."`
        log "Completed A Chart Beneath the Bell. Received 680 gold. A salvager has recovered a bell-shaped brass token from a wreck that should be three hundred years old."
